From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:02:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] packaging: keep source provenance separate from
 immutable archives

Record the reviewed upstream source and retain the peer-compatible SHA-derived package build workflow. Pin the published dependency set needed by the source build. Publish verified archives directly in the distribution repository, preserving existing URLs and manifest bytes while keeping package data out of the semantic source train. Document the maintained adoption contracts and source/history reconstruction workflow.

Provision uv in the package workflow for the upstream Python prepack builder.

Refresh the source train to upstream 1.49.0 and run CI on Node.js 22.
Retain staged-validator checks for actual deployments while codegen uses
non-committing analysis. Preserve native resident selection and upstream
mutation file access beside typed runtime value syscalls.

Install with ordinary npm peer dependency resolution.
